{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This describes how to receive messages with JMS in Spring."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "While JMS is typically associated with asynchronous processing, you can consume messages synchronously. The overloaded "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "receive(..)"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " methods provide this functionality. During a synchronous receive, the calling thread blocks until a message becomes available. This can be a dangerous operation, since the calling thread can potentially be blocked indefinitely. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "receiveTimeout"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " property specifies how long the receiver should wait before giving up waiting for a message."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jms-receiving-sync",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Synchronous Reception"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Spring also supports annotated-listener endpoints through the use of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@JmsListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotation and provides an open infrastructure to register endpoints programmatically. This is, by far, the most convenient way to setup an asynchronous receiver. See "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Enable Listener Endpoint Annotations"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "integration/jms/annotated.html#jms-annotated-support"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for more details."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In a fashion similar to a Message-Driven Bean (MDB) in the EJB world, the Message-Driven POJO (MDP) acts as a receiver for JMS messages. The one restriction (but see "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Using "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "integration/jms/receiving.html#jms-receiving-async-message-listener-adapter"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") on an MDP is that it must implement the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "jakarta.jms.MessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface. Note that, if your POJO receives messages on multiple threads, it is important to ensure that your implementation is thread-safe."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following example shows a simple implementation of an MDP:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./ExampleListener[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Once you have implemented your "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", it is time to create a message listener container."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following example shows how to define and configure one of the message listener containers that ships with Spring (in this case, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "DefaultMessageListenerContainer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "):"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./JmsConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "See the Spring javadoc of the various message listener containers (all of which implement "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListenerContainer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/jms/listener/MessageListenerContainer.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") for a full description of the features supported by each implementation."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jms-receiving-async",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Asynchronous reception: Message-Driven POJOs"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SessionAwareMessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface is a Spring-specific interface that provides a similar contract to the JMS "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface but also gives the message-handling method access to the JMS "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Session"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " from which the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Message"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " was received. The following listing shows the definition of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SessionAwareMessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "package org.springframework.jms.listener;\n\npublic interface SessionAwareMessageListener {\n\n\tvoid onMessage(Message message, Session session) throws JMSException;\n}"
              }
            ],
            "language": "java",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can choose to have your MDPs implement this interface (in preference to the standard JMS "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface) if you want your MDPs to be able to respond to any received messages (by using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Session"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " supplied in the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "onMessage(Message, Session)"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method). All of the message listener container implementations that ship with Spring have support for MDPs that implement either the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SessionAwareMessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface. Classes that implement the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SessionAwareMessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " come with the caveat that they are then tied to Spring through the interface. The choice of whether or not to use it is left entirely up to you as an application developer or architect."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Note that the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "onMessage(..)"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SessionAwareMessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface throws "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JMSException"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". In contrast to the standard JMS "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface, when using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SessionAwareMessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface, it is the responsibility of the client code to handle any thrown exceptions."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jms-receiving-async-session-aware-message-listener",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Using the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "SessionAwareMessageListener"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " Interface"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " class is the final component in Spring’s asynchronous messaging support. In a nutshell, it lets you expose almost any class as an MDP (though there are some constraints)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Consider the following interface definition:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./MessageDelegate[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Notice that, although the interface extends neither the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " nor the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SessionAwareMessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface, you can still use it as an MDP by using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " class. Notice also how the various message handling methods are strongly typed according to the contents of the various "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Message"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " types that they can receive and handle."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Now consider the following implementation of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageDelegate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./DefaultMessageDelegate[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In particular, note how the preceding implementation of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageDelegate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface (the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "DefaultMessageDelegate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " class) has no JMS dependencies at all. It truly is a POJO that we can make into an MDP through the following configuration:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./JmsConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The next example shows another MDP that can handle only receiving JMS "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "TextMessage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " messages. Notice how the message handling method is actually called "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "receive"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (the name of the message handling method in a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " defaults to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "handleMessage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "), but it is configurable (as you can see later in this section). Notice also how the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "receive(..)"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method is strongly typed to receive and respond only to JMS "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "TextMessage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " messages. The following listing shows the definition of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "TextMessageDelegate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./TextMessageDelegate[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following listing shows a class that implements the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "TextMessageDelegate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " interface:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./DefaultTextMessageDelegate[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The configuration of the attendant "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " would then be as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./MessageListenerConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Note that, if the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "messageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " receives a JMS "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Message"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " of a type other than "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "TextMessage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "IllegalStateException"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is thrown (and subsequently swallowed). Another of the capabilities of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " class is the ability to automatically send back a response "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Message"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " if a handler method returns a non-void value. Consider the following interface and class:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./ResponsiveTextMessageDelegate[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./DefaultResponsiveTextMessageDelegate[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "DefaultResponsiveTextMessageDelegate"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in conjunction with a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", any non-null value that is returned from the execution of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "'receive(..)'"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method is (in the default configuration) converted into a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "TextMessage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". The resulting "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "TextMessage"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is then sent to the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Destination"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (if one exists) defined in the JMS "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Reply-To"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " property of the original "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Message"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or the default "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Destination"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " set on the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (if one has been configured). If no "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Destination"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is found, an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "InvalidDestinationException"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is thrown (note that this exception is not swallowed and propagates up the call stack)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jms-receiving-async-message-listener-adapter",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Using "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MessageListenerAdapter"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Invoking a message listener within a transaction requires only reconfiguration of the listener container."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can activate local resource transactions through the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "sessionTransacted"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " flag on the listener container definition. Each message listener invocation then operates within an active JMS transaction, with message reception rolled back in case of listener execution failure. Sending a response message (through "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SessionAwareMessageListener"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") is part of the same local transaction, but any other resource operations (such as database access) operate independently. This usually requires duplicate message detection in the listener implementation, to cover the case where database processing has committed but message processing failed to commit."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Consider the following bean definition:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./JmsConfiguration[tag=snippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To participate in an externally managed transaction, you need to configure a transaction manager and use a listener container that supports externally managed transactions (typically, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "DefaultMessageListenerContainer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To configure a message listener container for XA transaction participation, you want to configure a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JtaTransactionManager"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (which, by default, delegates to the Jakarta EE server’s transaction subsystem). Note that the underlying JMS "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ConnectionFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " needs to be XA-capable and properly registered with your JTA transaction coordinator. (Check your Jakarta EE server’s configuration of JNDI resources.) This lets message reception as well as (for example) database access be part of the same transaction (with unified commit semantics, at the expense of XA transaction log overhead)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following bean definition creates a transaction manager:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./ExternalTxJmsConfiguration[tag=transactionManagerSnippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Then we need to add it to our earlier container configuration. The container takes care of the rest. The following example shows how to do so:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./ExternalTxJmsConfiguration[tag=jmsContainerSnippet,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jms-tx-participation",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Processing Messages Within Transactions"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Receiving a Message"
      }
    ]
  }
}
